      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    from scipy.optimize import brentq\n\n    bond_price = 950\n    cash_flows = [50, 50, 1050]\n    spot_rates = [0.015, 0.018, 0.020]\n    periods = [1, 2, 3]\n\n    def pv_difference(z_spread):\n        present_value = sum(\n            cash_flow / (1 + (spot_rate + z_spread) / 2) ** (2 * period)\n            for cash_flow, spot_rate, period\n            in zip(cash_flows, spot_rates, periods)\n        )\n        return present_value - bond_price\n\n    z_spread = brentq(pv_difference, -0.10, 0.20)\n    answer = round(z_spread * 100, 2)\n\n    return answer\n```",
